[wsg_run_one] PCEA statement_timeout=0
PCEA BLOCKED (link#227) — 2 blocking dam(s) on PCEA's downstream flow path have not been modelled yet.

link computes accessibility by reading ALREADY-PERSISTED downstream barriers.
Running PCEA now would mark segments accessible that are in fact dammed off, and exit 0.

  persist schema : zz326_default_pre
  unmodelled blocking dams downstream of PCEA:
    UPCE  320902cd-48fc-40e5-8c0f-191086f332aa   Peace Canyon Dam (psc 1)
    UPCE  957546a9-e6c7-46bf-947a-b17d8a818d71   Site C Dam (psc 1)
  model these first, DS-first: LPCE, UPCE

Fix — pick one:
  1. Model the downstream WSGs first:
       for w in LPCE UPCE; do Rscript data-raw/wsg_run_one.R $w <config>; done
  2. Model PCEA now and settle access after they land:
       Rscript data-raw/wsg_recompute_one.R PCEA <config>
  3. Override, if those dams are known passable / remediated / irrelevant.
     Recorded in the run log and surfaced by lnk_log_read():
       LNK_GUARD_DOWNSTREAM_NOTE="..." Rscript data-raw/wsg_run_one.R PCEA <config>

